# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_combined_recall.py" "COMBINED RECALL GATE: PASS" "combined recall (graph ∪ co-change vs correction-incident ground truth)" "combined recall: the product's #1 honest credibility number -- of the file-pairs that REAL CORRECTION INCIDENTS (revert/fix/bug/hotfix/regression commits touching >=2 files) had to touch together, what fraction does (a) the static code-graph adjacency catch, (b) the shipping co-change detector catch, (c) the UNION catch -- and what is the dominant MISS. This gate proves the measurement LOGIC deterministically on a TINY git-free in-memory synthetic scenario (no git, no Postgres): combined recall = |union ∩ incident| / |incident| (EXACT set-union semantics, NEVER an average); combined recall >= max(graph, co-change) (a union can only help); a pair caught ONLY by co-change (graph-INVISIBLE, no edge) LIFTS combined above graph-only (the second detector's value); the miss-classifier buckets an uncovered CROSS-DIR no-edge incident pair into no_graph_edge_xdir and a no-history-endpoint pair into no_history (co-change is structurally blind there). CONTENT-FREE is structurally enforced: the gate asserts tests/combined_recall.py opens NO repo file (no open/read_text/read_bytes), uses git --name-only (paths) + %s (commit SUBJECT only, for the boolean correction-pattern match) and NEVER requests commit bodies (%b) or diffs (-p/--patch/-u). The real tool (tests/combined_recall.py /repo) mirrors recall_measure.py's dampened adjacency (hub dampening + <=3 def fan-out + stoplist) VERBATIM and reuses _cg_cochange.cochange_pairs (the shipping co-change), so the printed numbers closely approximate (do not exactly replicate) what the SHIPPING engine warns on -- the exact stoplist lives in db/schema/70_social.sql, synced to the backtest by gate 154; the tool's copy is a close approximation -- not a flattering looser adjacency. Honest boundary printed: the incident ground truth is itself a proxy (message heuristic imperfect; not all coupling surfaces as reverts/fixes)" "combined recall: |union ∩ incident|/|incident| with exact set-union semantics (never an average), combined >= max(graph, co-change), a graph-invisible co-change pair lifts combined, the miss-classifier buckets cross-dir no-edge + no-history pairs correctly, and the tool is content-free (paths + git --name-only/%s only, no file contents, no %b/patch)" 20
